l websites."><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/identity.css"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/images/portfolio-icon-180.png"><link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest"></head><body data-page="on-page-seo-guide.html" class="academy page-lesson master-refresh"><header class="academy-header" id="top"><a class="academy-brand personal-brand" href="/"><span>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Personal Digital Portfolio · MBK Global</small></span></a><button class="academy-menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="academy-nav">Menu <span>+</span></button><nav id="academy-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href='/about'>About</a><a href='/projects'>Projects</a><a href='/services'>Services</a><a class='header-cta' href='/hire-me'>Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="portfolio-more"><summary>More</summary><div class="portfolio-panel"><section><h2>Professional work</h2><a href='/case-studies'>Case Studies</a><a href='/changelog'>Projects Changelog</a><a href='/delivered-project'>Process</a><a href='/resources'>Resources</a><a href='/news'>Notes</a></section><section><h2>Contact &amp; career</h2><a href='/book-a-call'>Book a Call</a><a href='/resume'>Resume / CV</a><a href='/hire-me'>Hire Me</a></section><section><h2>Content &amp; media</h2><a href='/gallery'>Gallery</a><a href='/blog'>Blog &amp; Articles</a><a href='/faq'>FAQs</a></section><section><h2>Personal brand</h2><a href='/about-muhammad-bakhtawar-khan'>Founder Profile</a><a href='/social'>Social Profiles</a><a href='/official-links'>Official Links</a></section></div></details><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch color theme">◐</button></nav></header>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
<main class="container academy-main" id="main-content"><section class="academy-page-hero"><div class="academy-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href='/blog'>Learning library</a></div><div class="academy-kicker">lesson <span> / MBK GLOBAL</span></div><h1>On-Page SEO Guide for Small Websites</h1><p>A clear on-page process helps visitors and search systems understand what each page offers. Start with the reader’s task, then make the page easy to scan and technically consistent.</p></section><div class="academy-reading-layout"><aside class="academy-toc"><p class="academy-kicker">IN THIS GUIDE</p><nav aria-label="On this page"><a href="#section-1"><span>01</span>Start with one clear search intent</a><a href="#section-2"><span>02</span>Write useful titles and descriptions</a><a href="#section-3"><span>03</span>Use a logical heading structure</a><a href="#section-4"><span>04</span>Make internal links descriptive</a><a href="#section-5"><span>05</span>Review images and canonical URLs</a></nav><div class="academy-author"><img src="/assets/images/mbk-personal-favicon-96.png" width="38" height="38" alt=""><div>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Founder, MBK Global</small></div></div><p class="academy-read-note">2 min read · Practical learning notes<br>Learn. Apply. Make it your own.</p><a class='academy-text-link' href='/resources'>More learning resources ↗</a></aside><div class="academy-reading-body"><article class="content-page"><header><p class="eyebrow">MBK Global · Practical guide</p></header><section><h2 id="section-1">Start with one clear search intent</h2><p>Choose the main question a page answers. Keep each page focused on a distinct need rather than repeating the same broad topic across multiple URLs. Check search results and your own site inventory before creating a new page.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-2">Write useful titles and descriptions</h2><p>Give every indexable page a descriptive, unique title and a concise summary that accurately represents its content. Treat the description as a useful search-result preview, not a guaranteed ranking signal. Avoid repetitive keyword strings and unsupported claims.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-3">Use a logical heading structure</h2><p>Use one clear H1 for the page’s main subject, followed by H2 sections and H3 subsections where needed. Headings should describe the content that follows, not serve as styling-only labels.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-4">Make internal links descriptive</h2><p>Link related pages where the next step is genuinely useful. Prefer anchor text such as “technical SEO checklist” over vague phrases like “click here.” Fix broken links and avoid orphaning useful pages.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-5">Review images and canonical URLs</h2><p>Write alt text for meaningful images based on their purpose; use empty alt text for decorative images. Keep canonical URLs absolute and consistent with internal links, redirects, social metadata and the sitemap.</p></section>
<p><strong>About this guide:</strong> This is general educational guidance. Adapt recommendations to your site's actual stack, risk and audience, and verify changes before publishing.</p>
<p>Explore related work: <a href='/web-development'>web development</a>, <a href='/projects'>projects</a>, and <a href='/contact'>contact</a>.</p></article></div></div><div data-portrait-track data-caption="The person behind the work"></div></main>
